 "notes": "Policy->group binding: a group attachment whose planned group is the stated group name must reference the content-matched policy (planned policy text, or declared text when the planned JSON is unknown), or an inline aws_iam_group_policy on that group carries the content. A policy built from a data.aws_iam_policy_document is matched through its planned JSON. Policy names are stated in quotes in the prompt, so they are detail checks. The dev/prod tag conditions must use a StringEquals/StringLike operator (a StringNotEquals on env=dev contradicts 'equal to'). The explicit-allow actions are bound to a policy attached to the administrators group, like the NotAction check. The Effect of the NotAction statement is not checked (key order in hand-written JSON varies, so binding Allow to the NotAction statement by regex would reject valid forms); a Deny NotAction statement would pass admin_policy_notaction."
